# Files for DOS and Windows 1.x-3.0 must keep their exact bytes.  Without these
# rules a "text=auto" setting (such as a global "* text=auto eol=lf") treats any
# of them without NUL bytes as text and stores CR LF as LF: for example the
# Windows 1 .GRB/.LGO files (a file name, CR LF, Ctrl-Z) and the README.TXT and
# OEMSETUP.INF files on the driver disks.

# DOS and Windows binaries, disk images, pictures
*.[Gg][Rr][Bb] binary
*.[Ll][Gg][Oo] binary
*.[Gg][Rr][23] binary
*.[Rr][Ll][Ee] binary
*.[Dd][Rr][Vv] binary
*.[Cc][Oo][Mm] binary
*.[Ee][Xx][Ee] binary
*.[Ff][Oo][Nn] binary
*.[Ii][Mm][Gg] binary
*.[Pp][Cc][Xx] binary
*.[Bb][Mm][Pp] binary
*.[Pp][Nn][Gg] binary

# Text files for the driver disks: CR LF line ends, kept as they are
**/drivers/*.[Tt][Xx][Tt] -text
**/drivers/*.[Ii][Nn][Ff] -text
